  "guid": "com.tyfon.discarder",
  "name": "Discarder",
  "slug": "discarder",
  "teaser": "Multi-select discard for UI Fixes",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2378.png",
  "downloads": 13509,
  "favourites_count": 22,
  "description": "<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Description</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h3>Requires <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/1342/ui-fixes\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">UI Fixes</a>! You must have UI Fixes installed for this mod to do anything.</h3>\n<p>Adds the ability to discard multiple items at once, in and out of raid, when multi-selecting items with UI Fixes. You must have UI Fixes installed and the multi-select feature enabled (which it is by default)</p>\n<p>This is a separate mod from UI Fixes because:</p>\n<p>1. I wanted a proof of concept for the mulit-select interop</p>\n<p>2. Force you to opt-in to a feature that could delete half your stash if you use it that way.</p>\n<p>No configuration required. You will still get a single confirmation dialog when discarding items out of raid.</p>\n<p>If you install this mod and use it to delete items, then complain that it deleted items, you have no one to blame but yourself.</p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Installation</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>Like almost every mod here, extract the zip archive into your SPT directory.</p>\n<p>Example (thanks DrakiaXYZ for the gif)</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vKRw58b.gif\" alt=\"vKRw58b.gif\" /></p>\n<h3>Uninstallation</h3>\n<p>To uninstall, simply delete <strong>Tyfon.Discarder.dll</strong> from <strong>&lt;your SPT folder&gt;/BepInEx/plugins</strong></p></div></div></div>\n<p>If you’d like to support my work, you can <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/tyfon\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">buy me a coffee</a> ☕</p>\n",
